17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348071 #edb/ref 1071 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-60 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348071 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d4333e7-3a3e-56f4-8135-82a56303935f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348071 #edb/ref 1074 "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-60 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{3}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348074 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348074 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78337" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348074 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348074 #edb/ref 1071 "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 17\\end{bmatrix}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348074 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4db462f3-5435-5b8e-8538-abab7a997273" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348074 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=17.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $17.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186393814 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393814 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78294" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393814 #edb/ref 