96190 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e53a5dab-4c76-5167-b8bb-303aab059a57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396190 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we compute the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/4a/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a reflection in the line $y=-x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396191 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4259dafc-1a37-55ff-aa39-09cc98e980bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396192 #edb/ref 1080 "Dilation with scale factor $1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9fe2e6e8-335c-58be-b255-c60fa43a41f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396193 #edb/ref 1080 "Reflection across the $x$-axis" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396193 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396193 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7aa33fd0-bc88-5221-b0ce-b4b35cc3e471" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396194 #edb/ref 1080 "Reflection in the line $y=x$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396194 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396194 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "99f4a2a9-46a7-591a-b8d7-dd58887c39ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396195 #edb/ref 1080 "Reflection in the line $y=-x$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396195 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396195 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7810d358-12eb-5db3-8061-1d557a816ce3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396196 #edb/ref 1080 "Reflection across the $y$-axis" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396196 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396196 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "84c9888e-01f7-56a1-a9cc-589307e77959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396715 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396715 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396715 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396715 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following represents a reflection in the line $y=-x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396715 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a51c70cd-319b-5de1-a71f-816af37c3370" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396715 #edb/ref 1074 "The correct answer is $T=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{b